{"blocks":[["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/","source-block-723","Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials/Character/Pantalaimon",["His Dark Materials","Characters"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/","source-block-806","Concepts",["His Dark Materials"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/","source-block-821","Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials/Concept/Daemon",["His Dark Materials","Concepts"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/","source-block-897","Links",["His Dark Materials"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/","source-block-909","Wikipedia",["His Dark Materials","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/1/95/The%20Golden%20Compass/","source-block-129","Northern Lights / The Golden Compass",[]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/1/95/The%20Golden%20Compass/","source-block-235","About",["Northern Lights / The Golden Compass"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/1/95/The%20Golden%20Compass/","source-block-247","First book of Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials. UK title Northern Lights (1995); North American title The Golden Compass.",["Northern Lights / The Golden Compass","About"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/1/95/The%20Golden%20Compass/","source-block-401","Links",["Northern Lights / The Golden Compass"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/1/95/The%20Golden%20Compass/","source-block-413","Wikipedia",["Northern Lights / The Golden Compass","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/1/95/The%20Golden%20Compass/","source-block-492","Person/Philip Pullman",["Northern Lights / The Golden Compass","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/2/97/The%20Subtle%20Knife/","source-block-129","The Subtle Knife",[]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/2/97/The%20Subtle%20Knife/","source-block-200","About",["The Subtle Knife"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/2/97/The%20Subtle%20Knife/","source-block-212","Second book of Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials.",["The Subtle Knife","About"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/2/97/The%20Subtle%20Knife/","source-block-289","Links",["The Subtle Knife"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/2/97/The%20Subtle%20Knife/","source-block-301","Wikipedia",["The Subtle Knife","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/2/97/The%20Subtle%20Knife/","source-block-365","Person/Philip Pullman",["The Subtle Knife","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/3/00/The%20Amber%20Spyglass/","source-block-129","The Amber Spyglass",[]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/3/00/The%20Amber%20Spyglass/","source-block-204","About",["The Amber Spyglass"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/3/00/The%20Amber%20Spyglass/","source-block-216","Third book of Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials.",["The Amber Spyglass","About"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/3/00/The%20Amber%20Spyglass/","source-block-292","Links",["The Amber Spyglass"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/3/00/The%20Amber%20Spyglass/","source-block-304","Wikipedia",["The Amber Spyglass","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/3/00/The%20Amber%20Spyglass/","source-block-370","Person/Philip Pullman",["The Amber Spyglass","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Lyra%20Belacqua/","source-block-91","Lyra Belacqua",[]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Lyra%20Belacqua/","source-block-156","About",["Lyra Belacqua"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Lyra%20Belacqua/","source-block-168","Protagonist of Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials; also called Lyra Silvertongue. Reads the alethiometer and travels between worlds with Will Parry. Her dæmon is Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials/Character/Pantalaimon.",["Lyra Belacqua","About"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Lyra%20Belacqua/","source-block-437","Appears in",["Lyra Belacqua"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Lyra%20Belacqua/","source-block-454","Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials",["Lyra Belacqua","Appears in"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Lyra%20Belacqua/","source-block-515","Links",["Lyra Belacqua"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Lyra%20Belacqua/","source-block-527","Wikipedia",["Lyra Belacqua","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Lyra%20Belacqua/","source-block-588","Person/Philip Pullman",["Lyra Belacqua","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Pantalaimon/","source-block-119","Pantalaimon",[]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Pantalaimon/","source-block-203","About",["Pantalaimon"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Pantalaimon/","source-block-215","Dæmon of Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials/Character/Lyra Belacqua in Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials; also called Pan. An example of a Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials/Concept/Daemon. Named from Greek Panteleimon, \"all-compassionate.\" He first appears as a dark brown moth; favored forms include a snow-white ermine, a wildcat, and a mouse; he settles as a red-gold pine marten with a cream-white throat.",["Pantalaimon","About"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Pantalaimon/","source-block-700","Appears in",["Pantalaimon"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Pantalaimon/","source-block-717","Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials",["Pantalaimon","Appears in"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Pantalaimon/","source-block-778","Links",["Pantalaimon"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Pantalaimon/","source-block-790","Fandom",["Pantalaimon","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Character/Pantalaimon/","source-block-869","Person/Philip Pullman",["Pantalaimon","Links"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-215","Dæmon",[]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-291","Overview",["Dæmon"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-306","A dæmon is a person's inner self made external as an animal: it speaks, advises, and has a life that walks beside its human.",["Dæmon","Overview"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-440","It matters because Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials treats a person as something that can walk beside you — identity made visible, answerable, and able to settle.",["Dæmon","Overview"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-633","Context",["Dæmon"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-647","In Lyra's world a dæmon is a person's nature given an animal body, usually of the opposite sex. Children's dæmons shift form; at adulthood they settle into the animal that fits the person's character.",["Dæmon","Context"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-856","Pullman's pictures for the idea include portraits where a sitter and a small animal share a psychological link — Leonardo's Lady with an Ermine, Holbein's Lady with a Squirrel and a Starling, Tiepolo's Young Woman with a Macaw — and Socrates' daimon, an inner voice given a body.",["Dæmon","Context"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-1152","This garden already reaches for the idea when talking about a Horcrux: both are ways a person's essence lives outside the body. A Horcrux hides a torn fragment in an object. A dæmon is the person, walking and talking beside them.",["Dæmon","Context"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-1393","Key Principles",["Dæmon"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-1414","Companion-soul — human and dæmon are one life in two bodies, not a pet and its owner. Kill the dæmon and the human dies; when the human dies the dæmon fades.",["Dæmon","Key Principles"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-1585","Settling is coming of age — form becomes fixed as identity does.",["Dæmon","Key Principles"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-1660","Distance is injury — a human and dæmon must stay near each other; forced separation is agony, and far enough apart it kills. Witches, shamans, and (after the Land of the Dead) some others can travel farther because they have already survived that tearing.",["Dæmon","Key Principles"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-1927","Mechanism",["Dæmon"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-1943","Children's dæmons change form at will. At adolescence the form locks to the animal that matches character.",["Dæmon","Mechanism"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-2055","For a human to touch another person's dæmon is taboo; dæmons may touch one another, and those contacts show the relationship between the humans.",["Dæmon","Mechanism"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-2206","Permanent tearing of human from dæmon (intercision) releases a burst of energy and usually kills; it is the method the General Oblation Board uses in the first book.",["Dæmon","Mechanism"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-2377","Examples",["Dæmon"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-2392","Person/Philip Pullman/Book/Series/His Dark Materials/Character/Pantalaimon — Lyra Belacqua's dæmon; also called Pan. Favored changing forms include a dark brown moth and a snow-white ermine; he settles as a red-gold pine marten with a cream-white throat.",["Dæmon","Examples"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-2658","Horcrux — the garden's other picture of identity stored outside the body; murder-made fragment versus living companion.",["Dæmon","Examples"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-2788","Misconceptions",["Dæmon"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-2809","\"A dæmon is a familiar or a pet\" — False; it is the person externalized.",["Dæmon","Misconceptions"]],["Person/Philip%20Pullman/Book/Series/His%20Dark%20Materials/Concept/Daemon/","source-block-2893","\"A dæmon is a separate character who happens to travel with someone\" — Oversimplified; they argue and can be parted, but they are not two people who met.",["Dæmon","Misconceptions"]],["Person/Philippe%20Mion/","source-block-65","Philippe Mion",[]],["Person/Philippe%20Mion/","source-block-83","Bio",["Philippe Mion"]],["Person/Philippe%20Mion/","source-block-93","Composer of acousmatic music",["Philippe Mion","Bio"]],["Person/Philippe%20Mion/","source-block-126","Notable Work",["Philippe Mion"]],["Person/Philippe%20Mion/","source-block-145","Confidence",["Philippe Mion","Notable Work"]],["Person/Philippe%20Mion/Confidence/","source-block-0","Confidence",[]],["Person/phiresky/","source-block-41","Person/phiresky",[]],["Person/phiresky/","source-block-61","Bio",["Person/phiresky"]]],"format_version":5}